  "worked_solution": "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an odd function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=1$ and we are already given the coefficients ${b}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)\u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-1,1).$ \nTherefore, the $2$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}(-4t)\\,\\text{d}t & \u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(n\\pi t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ [-2{t}^{2}]_{0}^{x} & \u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\pi t)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ -2{x}^{2} & \u223c{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{8(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(n\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
